{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791346124266,"sessionID":"ses_eeb7537e0ffe7TnNRtM3LzuDXr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"q3p9RzqKQC7Gs2mO","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/user/auto-psych/src/pipelines/outer_loop/projects/rsa_reference/data/README.md","offset":60,"limit":100},"output":"<path>/home/user/auto-psych/src/pipelines/outer_loop/projects/rsa_reference/data/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n60: | `familiarization` | JSON per-object counts out of 9 familiarization images (E5 only), else empty |\n61: | `grayscale` | JSON per-object 1 = shown in greyscale (E7 and its rerun only), else empty |\n62: | `dv` | `forced_choice`, `betting`, `likert`, `production` |\n63: | `choice` | chosen object index (forced choice) |\n64: | `response` | betting: JSON dollars per object (sum 100); likert: JSON 1-7 per object; production: JSON `{\"modality\", \"description\"` or the four checkbox booleans`, \"overspec\"}`; the speaker level-1 listener trials (no matrix): `{\"choice_role\": ...}` |\n65: | `referent` | production: index of the object the speaker had to describe |\n66: | `included` | `True` when the participant passes the exclusion criteria of the analysis Rmd that reads the file |\n67: | `exclusion_reason` | `;`-joined: `manip_check_target`, `manip_check_dist`, `name_check`, `duplicate_participant`, `overspec_missing` |\n68: | `notes` | `;`-joined flags for anything inferred or unrecorded on that row (listed under Known gaps) |\n69: \n70: ## Rows per experiment\n71: \n72: participants (included) / rows (included) / condition rows (included):\n73: \n74: | experiment | series | participants | rows | conditions |\n75: |---|---|---|---|---|\n76: | E1_dv | 1-prelims/dv | 689 (554) | 689 (554) | forced_choice 290 (248); betting 199 (158); likert 200 (148) |\n77: | E2_manip_check | 1-prelims/manip | 580 (513) | 580 (513) | manip_check 340 (306); no_manip_check 240 (207) |\n78: | E3_ling_frame | 1-prelims/linguistic_framing | 100 (89) | 100 (89) | one_word 57 (51); my_X_has 43 (38) |\n79: | E4_prior_frame | 2-prior/measurement | 200 (175) | 200 (175) | mumble 104 (88); action 96 (87) |\n80: | E5_baserate | 2-prior/baserates | 800 (488) | 800 (488) | inference_baserate_{0.11,0.33,0.44,0.77} 100 (72), 93 (63), 107 (68), 100 (75); prior_baserate_{...} 96 (53), 103 (57), 99 (49), 102 (51) |\n81: | E6_valence | 2-prior/language | 550 (478) | 550 (478) | favorite 200 (176); least_favorite 100 (86); favorite_prior 116 (100); least_favorite_prior 134 (116) |\n82: | E7_color | 2-prior/color | 300 (264) | 300 (264) | inference_color_{none,foil,logical,target} 42 (38), 53 (47), 54 (48), 51 (46); prior_color_{foil,logical,target} 31 (27), 27 (24), 42 (34) |\n83: | color_prior_rerun | 2-prior/color | 100 (83) | 100 (83) | prior_color_{foil,logical,target} 34 (30), 30 (24), 36 (29) |\n84: | E8_levels | 3-levels/levels | 416 (345) | 416 (345) | simple_L0 65 (49); simple_L1 55 (46); complex_L0 62 (52); complex_L1 65 (58); complex_L2 73 (62); complex_prior 96 (78) |\n85: | levels_prior_action | 3-levels/levels | 104 (91) | 104 (91) | complex_prior_action 104 (91) |\n86: | E9_twins | 3-levels/twins | 220 (193) | 220 (193) | twin 49 (46); uniform 71 (60); prior 100 (87) |\n87: | E10_oddman | 3-levels/oddman | 300 (269) | 300 (269) | patch 102 (93); word 98 (89); prior 100 (87) |\n88: | size | 3-levels/size | 1750 (1368) | 1750 (1368) | 13 inference conditions `inference_<N>obj_<F>feat_sl<k>` (1300 rows, 985 incl.); 9 prior matrices `prior_<N>obj_<F>feat` (450, 383) |\n89: | sequences | 4-sequences | 500 (477) | 1800 (1710) | 1w0w1b 345 (333); 0w1w1b 255 (240); (0w1w)x3 300 (282); (0b1b)x3 300 (276); 0w1w2w 138 (129); 2w1w0w 162 (159); 0w2w1w 135 (135); 1w2w0w 165 (156) |\n90: | speakers | 5-speakers | 1356 (1166) | 2259 (1949) | L1:{text,checkbox,virtual_keyboard} 149 (121), 150 (136), 154 (126); seq_L1:{...} 302 (264), 300 (254), 304 (270); seq_L2:{...} 300 (270), 300 (272), 300 (236) (seq rows = 2 per participant) |\n91: \n92: ## How the data reproduce the paper\n93: \n94: * **models.csv / prior_counts.csv.** Aggregating the included forced-choice\n95:   rows of each `paper_cond`, mapping each chosen object to the\n96:   `models/matrices.R` row with the same features (a choice of one of two\n97:   identical twins counts half for each, as models.csv does), reproduces every\n98:   row of `prior_counts.csv` and every `n` and every count of `models.csv`\n99:   except two cells, which models.csv labels differently from the stimuli:\n100:   * `complex` cond `1` (\"mustache\"): the data are 44 M, 11 GM, 3 HG.\n101:     models.csv has `foil`(M) 44, `logical`(HG) 11, `target`(GM) 3, i.e. it puts\n102:     the 11 literally-true GM choices on HG, which has no mustache.\n103:   * `simple` cond `0` (\"hat\"): the data are 48 HG, 1 featureless face, 0 G.\n104:     models.csv has the 1 on `target`(G) and 0 on `foil`.\n105:   Both come from the hand relabelling in `models/data/levels_mod.csv`, which\n106:   gave each of these cells the other's permutation. levels.csv and prior.csv\n107:   (the Rmds' own output, by role label) are reproduced exactly, all cells. For\n108:   the comparison, the CSV's columns are matrices.R's `hat, glasses` (simple),\n109:   `hat, glasses, mustache` (complex, twins) and `hat, mustache, glasses`\n110:   (oddman, so that twin_1 is matrices.R's `logical` and twin_2 its `foil`, as\n111:   levels.Rmd maps them).\n112: * **Table 1.** N_total matches for all ten experiments. N_include matches for\n113:   E1-E5. For E6-E10 Table 1 counts participants passing the manipulation and\n114:   name checks *before* repeat participants are removed: 502 = 478 + 24,\n115:   267 = 264 + 3, 362 = 345 + 17, 194 = 193 + 1, 270 = 269 + 1 (the second\n116:   term is the participants excluded only as duplicates). The analyses and\n117:   models.csv do remove them, and so does the CSV.\n118: * The commented-out rows of the table (size 1750/1368, sequences, production)\n119:   also match, with two labels swapped there: \"Level 1 x3 200/193\" is the two\n120:   level-2 sequence files and \"Level 2 100/93\" the two x3 files; the production\n121:   \"Level 1\" N_total of 450 is nominal (the files hold 453).\n122: \n123: ## Coding decisions\n124: \n125: **Matrices.** Every one-shot listener display is one `scale_and_level`\n126: condition of `pragmods_parameter_setter_c1.js` (langcog/pragmods-expts\n127: `8ff10c3`), transcribed in `C1` in the ingest. `objects` are its unpermuted\n128: `expt` rows; a column present on no object (the third feature of the simple\n129: matrix, never shown on any object) is dropped.\n130: \n131: | scale_and_level | matrix | objects (roles) | uttered column |\n132: |---|---|---|---|\n133: | 0 | simple, level 0 | 00 foil, 01 logical, 11 target | col 0 (only on target) |\n134: | 1 | simple, level 1 (the standard game) | 00 foil, 01 target, 11 logical | col 1 |\n135: | 2-4 | complex (M, GM, HG) levels 0-2 | 001, 011, 110 | 2: col 0 (HG); 3: col 2 (M); 4: col 1 (GM) |\n136: | 5-7 | twins | 011 single, 101 twin, 101 twin | 5: prior; 6: col 0; 7: col 2 (on all) |\n137: | 8 | oddman | 011 twin_1, 101 twin_2, 110 odd_one | col 2 |\n138: \n139: The 2013 files (E1, the E6 favourite batches, LEAS) record no\n140: `scale_and_levels_condition`; `all_experiments.csv` gives 1 for all of them\n141: (note `scale_and_level_1_from_all_experiments_csv`).\n142: \n143: **Display and feature names** are solved jointly from whatever a file records\n144: (`target_position`, `logical_position`, `{target,logical,foil}_property`,\n145: `left/middle/right_items`, `position_chosen`/`items_chosen`,\n146: `position_with_color`): every layout of the matrix consistent with all of it is\n147: enumerated, and a position or word is filled only where all agree. A file\n148: whose records admit no layout raises. Layouts that differ only by swapping\n149: identical objects (twins) or identically distributed features are one layout:\n150: identical objects are placed in index order left to right. The c1 code's\n151: `logical_position` is the position of its \"distractor\", which is always the\n152: `logical` row.\n153: \n154: **Queries.** `question_type` 0 with a word (`linguistic_framing` 0-6, 10, 13,\n155: 14) or the colour patch (9) is `utterance`; 0 with framing 7/8 (silent\n156: favourite / least favourite), 1 and 3 (mumble), 2 and 4 are `prior`.\n157: \n158: **Exclusions** follow each analysis block of the Rmds: the manipulation checks\n159: (`manip_check_target`/`_dist` against the counts each condition requires),\n\n(Showing lines 60-159 of 475. Use offset=160 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"| `familiarization` | JSON per-object counts out of 9 familiarization images (E5 only), else empty |\n| `grayscale` | JSON per-object 1 = shown in greyscale (E7 and its rerun only), else empty |\n| `dv` | `forced_choice`, `betting`, `likert`, `production` |\n| `choice` | chosen object index (forced choice) |\n| `response` | betting: JSON dollars per object (sum 100); likert: JSON 1-7 per object; production: JSON `{\"modality\", \"description\"` or the four checkbox booleans`, \"overspec\"}`; the speaker level-1 listener trials (no matrix): `{\"choice_role\": ...}` |\n| `referent` | production: index of the object the speaker had to describe |\n| `included` | `True` when the participant passes the exclusion criteria of the analysis Rmd that reads the file |\n| `exclusion_reason` | `;`-joined: `manip_check_target`, `manip_check_dist`, `name_check`, `duplicate_participant`, `overspec_missing` |\n| `notes` | `;`-joined flags for anything inferred or unrecorded on that row (listed under Known gaps) |\n\n## Rows per experiment\n\nparticipants (included) / rows (included) / condition rows (included):\n\n| experiment | series | participants | rows | conditions |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| E1_dv | 1-prelims/dv | 689 (554) | 689 (554) | forced_choice 290 (248); betting 199 (158); likert 200 (148) |\n| E2_manip_ch